cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use sc-markers, please cite it and the works it builds on, listed under references (the methods it uses and, when you ran it on it, the demo dataset)."
type: software
version: "0.1.2"
title: sc-markers
abstract: >-
  A Pennsieve processor of the single-cell workflows: marker genes per cell type or cluster from
  single-cell or single-nucleus RNA-seq, with scanpy's Wilcoxon rank-sum test on log-normalized
  expression pooled across samples, filtered for effect size, detection and consistency across
  samples; writes a ranked marker table, a dot plot, a heatmap and a summary for the report.
authors:
  - name: Pennsieve (University of Pennsylvania)
contact:
- given-names: Joost
  family-names: Wagenaar
  orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0004-5925-5451
  affiliation: University of Pennsylvania
repository-code: "https://github.com/pennsieve-apps/sc-markers"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - single-cell
  - single-nucleus
  - transcriptomics
  - marker genes
  - cell types
